* norg-diagram test file

  Cursor on a block, then `:NorgDiagramFloat` for the link view.
  `:NorgDiagramToggle` and `:Neorg toggle-concealer` should both reveal source.

** 1. Basic mermaid, no directives

   Plain render, everything on `hl`, borders on `edge_hl`.

@code mermaid
graph TD
A[Index] --> B[Projects]
A --> C[Journal]
@end

** 2. Basic d2

   Note d2 indents its output; the first line must line up with the rest.

@code d2
api: API
db: Postgres
api -> db: query
@end

** 3. Basic graph-easy
@code easy
[ q0 ] -- a --> [ q1 ]
[ q1 ] -- b --> [ q1 ]
[ q1 ] -- a --> [ q2 ]
[ q2 ] -- a,b --> [ q2 ]
@end

** 3. Theme colors via ::: (mermaid only)

   No classDef lines: the preprocessor generates them. Labels only,
   since mermaid-ascii colors the text and not the box.

@code mermaid
graph LR
api[API]:::green --> db[Postgres]:::blue
api --> cache[Redis]:::red
@end

** 4. Explicit hex in classDef passes through untouched

@code mermaid
graph LR
classDef alarm color:#ff00ff
ok[Healthy] --> bad[Failing]:::alarm
@end

** 5. #color on a label

@code d2
api: API
db: Postgres
api -> db: query
#color API green
#color query red
@end

** 6. #color on a box

   The whole rectangle, including borders, should be blue.

@code d2
api: API
db: Postgres
api -> db
#color Postgres blue box
@end

** 7. Label and box, different colors, both orders

   Both should give a red box with a green label.

@code d2
api: API
db: Postgres
api -> db
#color API red box
#color API green
@end

@code d2
svc: Service
store: Store
svc -> store
#color Service green
#color Service red box
@end

** 8. ::: beats #color on the same label

   API stays green (from :::), its box turns red.

@code mermaid
graph LR
api[API]:::green --> db[Postgres]
%%color API red box
%%color API blue
@end

** 9. Three-node layout: the third box must be detected

   Redis sits lower than the others, so its box is on rows where the
   columns above contain connectors. All three boxes should be found.

@code mermaid
graph LR
api[API] --> db[Postgres]
api --> cache[Redis]
%%color Redis green box
@end

** 10. Links, mermaid

   `:NorgDiagramFloat` here: Tab cycles Index / Projects / Journal,
   <CR> follows.

@code mermaid
graph TD
A[Index] --> B[Projects]
A --> C[Journal]
%%link Index {:index:}
%%link Projects {:projects/overview:}
%%link Journal {:journal:** Today}
@end

** 11. Links, d2

@code d2
api: API
db: Postgres
api -> db: query
#link API {:services/api:}
#link Postgres {:services/db:}
@end

** 12. Links and colors together

   Directives of both kinds in one block; neither should leak into the
   source the renderer sees.

@code d2
api: API
db: Postgres
api -> db
#color API green box
#link API {:services/api:}
@end

** 13. Wide diagram, --max-width

   Should compact or clip at the window edge, not overflow. Resize the
   window and it should re-render.

@code mermaid
graph LR
A[Alpha] --> B[Bravo] --> C[Charlie] --> D[Delta] --> E[Echo] --> F[Foxtrot] --> G[Golf] --> H[Hotel]
@end

** 14. Broken source: error path

   Renderer stderr shown in `err_hl`, no crash, other blocks unaffected.

@code mermaid
graph LR
classDef
A --> B
@end

** 15. Unknown color name falls through

   `chartreuse` is neither a palette name nor a highlight group, so the
   directive is ignored and the label renders normally.

@code d2
api: API
#color API chartreuse
@end

** 16. Not a diagram: must be left completely alone

@code lua
local function hello()
	print("this block must never be rendered or concealed")
end
@end

** 17. Two blocks back to back, no blank line between

   Both diagrams must appear, stacked

@code mermaid
graph TD
U[One] --> V[Two]
@end
@code mermaid
graph TD
W[Three] --> X[Four]
@end

** 18. Trailing block at end of file

   Nothing follows, so the anchor falls back to the line above.

@code mermaid
graph LR
Last[Final] --> Node[Block]
@end
